From 401a062fd8de9d1d7241d8567272dc47508bc444 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StachowiakDawid <dawidos234@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:38:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/exynos: Exynos 9820 DSIM/DECON0 takeover and S6E3HA9
 panel drivers

Internal display of the Samsung Galaxy S10+ (SM-G975F): DECON0 -> DSIM
-> S6E3HA9 AMOLED panel in MIPI command mode. The pipeline is taken
over from the bootloader as it runs instead of being programmed from
scratch.

 - exynos9820_dsim_cmd: MIPI DSI host that adopts the running link and
   only transfers DCS commands, which is all the command mode panel
   needs once it is lit.
 - panel-samsung-s6e3ha9: 1440x3040 panel (AMB640TP01), inherited lit
   and not reset at probe. Backlight device; blank_mode selects what a
   blank does (display off only, or sleep in/out with a full re-init),
   power_off=1 cuts the supplies with reset asserted and does a full
   init on unblank; hold_dark keeps the panel dark over a wake that is
   not meant to light the screen. Sysfs: touch_sync (replays the TSP
   sync setup the touch controller needs) and dcs_dump (snapshot of
   the DDIC state). The bootloader's gamma/ELVSS/VINT registers are
   logged at probe.
 - exynos9820_decon: KMS driver for DECON0 with one primary plane.
   Page flips go through the shadow register update: the plane
   registers are written without masking the TE trigger, the update
   request is written inside a frame and only for the window, with a
   fallback to a global update if the IDMA does not latch. The fetch
   uses the IDMA ARGB codes like the bootloader. Vblank comes from the
   frame start interrupt, or from polling the frame counter if the
   interrupt is not delivered. CRTC off is a soft off (soft_off): the
   pipeline keeps running on the parked boot framebuffer and only the
   panel is blanked. Imported dma-bufs that would need bouncing are
   refused. The driver only binds with enable=1, so that loading the
   module does not take the screen away from simpledrm; fbdev
   emulation is optional (fbdev).

The bindings of the three devices are part of this commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: StachowiakDawid <dawidos234@gmail.com>
